From 1b248c57dbff2e5bbc64ab3c06d6e9463d759237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:35:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/57] target/arm: cortex-m0plus with the ARMv6-M MPU and
 unprivileged mode

A cortex-m0plus CPU type: the Cortex-M0 ISA with the Cortex-M0+ r0p1
CPUID, an 8-region MPU and the Unprivileged/Privileged extension, as
PIC32CM silicon has them (MPU_TYPE 0x800, CONTROL.nPRIV writable).

The ARMv6-M MPU uses the PMSAv7 register format and lookup
(arm_pmsav7_format()); on ARMv6-M, MPU_RASR has no TEX field and
MPU_RBAR.ADDR is [31:8], as read back on silicon. Plain cortex-m0 keeps
no MPU and its migration stream.

Fix in the PMSAv7 lookup: an access to a disabled subregion fell
through to a lower region or the background map with a whole-page TLB
entry, so later accesses to enabled subregions of the same page did not
fault.

The PIC32CM SoC and boards use cortex-m0plus instead of cortex-m0 with
a "midr" global. Board docs updated (CPU, EIC, TC, RTC, EVSYS, PORT
events).

Checked against PIC32CM MC00 silicon with firmware/hello/tests/mpu.c
(transcripts identical).

Peripheral Pretender: a personal project; not for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
